tecting when an agent has encountered novel conditions, and determining how it should adjust its actions. In this position paper we propose a framework that couples cognitive reasoning and generative algorithms by leveraging conflict detection to adjust to unexpected dynamics. Specifically, we propose that a metacognitive conflict resolution mechanism is necessary; such a mechanism would balance the use of commonsense and deliberative reasoning to allow the agent to navigate novel conditions."}]", "excerpt_truncated": true, "source_sha256": "f3b3db50ef97598e38088b5915a4c40bd52168910ef6479ae96354aac96aca07", "verification_required": true, "topic_domain": "unrecognized_reasoning_limits", "evidence_role": "discovery", "host_tier": "discovery", "source_identity": null, "persistent_identifiers": ["doi:10.1007/s10462-018-9646-y", "doi:10.1007/s10462-018-9646-y.pdf", "doi:10.1609/aaaiss.v2i1.27705", "openalex:W2883445328", "openalex:W4391117109"], "source_candidates": ["https://doi.org/10.1007/s10462-018-9646-y", "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10462-018-9646-y.pdf", "https://doi.org/10.1609/aaaiss.v2i1.27705"], "source_candidate_identities": {}}
